IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc1-part4-amounts`
IMPORT `uc1-part4-children-housing`

-- Tests of uc1-part4-children-housing.l4 (regulations 23 to 26). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the
-- regulation named in the comment beside it, and none was copied from the output of the rule.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 23(2): the elements included under section 12 of the Act are the LCWRA, carer and childcare costs elements.
#ASSERT `reg 23(2) — an element included under section 12 of the Act` `LCWRA element`
#ASSERT `reg 23(2) — an element included under section 12 of the Act` `carer element`
#ASSERT `reg 23(2) — an element included under section 12 of the Act` `childcare costs element`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(2) — an element included under section 12 of the Act` `standard allowance`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(2) — an element included under section 12 of the Act` `child element`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 23(2) — an element included under section 12 of the Act` `housing costs element`)

-- Regulation 23(1): the maximum amount is the sum of the elements (338.58 + 303.94 + 400 + 217.26 = 1259.78).
`an award with four elements` MEANS `Amounts of the elements of an award` WITH
    `the standard allowance` IS 338.58
    `the child element` IS 303.94
    `the housing costs element` IS 400
    `the LCWRA element` IS 217.26
    `the carer element` IS 0
    `the childcare costs element` IS 0
#ASSERT `reg 23(1) — the maximum amount of an award` `an award with four elements` EQUALS 1259.78

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 24(1) and (2): the child elements.
#ASSERT `reg 24 — the amount of the child elements` 0 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 24 — the amount of the child elements` 1 0 0 EQUALS 303.94
#ASSERT `reg 24 — the amount of the child elements` 2 0 0 EQUALS 607.88
-- three children, one with the lower rate (164.79) and one with the higher (514.71): 911.82 + 164.79 + 514.71.
#ASSERT `reg 24 — the amount of the child elements` 3 1 1 EQUALS 1591.32

-- (2): which rate of additional amount applies to one child or qualifying young person.
GIVEN benefits IS A LIST OF Benefit
      `care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `care component of child disability payment at the highest rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `certified as severely sight impaired or blind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `certified by a consultant ophthalmologist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Entitlements of a child or qualifying young person to the additional amount`
`test — a child with` benefits `care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate` `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate` `care component of child disability payment at the highest rate` `daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate` `daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate` `certified as severely sight impaired or blind` `certified by a consultant ophthalmologist` MEANS
    `Entitlements of a child or qualifying young person to the additional amount` WITH
        `entitled to` IS benefits
        `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS `care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate`
        `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate` IS `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate`
        `entitled to the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate` IS `care component of child disability payment at the highest rate`
        `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate` IS `daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate`
        `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate` IS `daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate`
        `sight certificate` IS `Sight certificate` WITH
            `certified as severely sight impaired or blind` IS `certified as severely sight impaired or blind`
            `certified by a consultant ophthalmologist` IS `certified by a consultant ophthalmologist`

`a child entitled to no benefit` MEANS `test — a child with` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a child entitled to disability living allowance only` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `disability living allowance`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a child entitled to personal independence payment only` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `personal independence payment`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a child entitled to disability living allowance with the care component at the highest rate` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `disability living allowance`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a child entitled to adult disability payment with the daily living component at the enhanced rate` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `adult disability payment`) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a child entitled to child disability payment with the care component at the highest rate` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `child disability payment`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a child entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance with the care component at the highest rate` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `Scottish adult disability living allowance`) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a child entitled to personal independence payment with the daily living component at the enhanced rate` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `personal independence payment`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a blind child entitled to no benefit` MEANS `test — a child with` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a child certified as blind but not by a consultant ophthalmologist` MEANS `test — a child with` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`a child entitled only to attendance allowance` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `attendance allowance`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a child entitled only to carer's allowance` MEANS `test — a child with` (LIST `carer's allowance`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled to no benefit` EQUALS `no additional amount`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled to disability living allowance only` EQUALS `the lower rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled to personal independence payment only` EQUALS `the lower rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled to disability living allowance with the care component at the highest rate` EQUALS `the higher rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled to adult disability payment with the daily living component at the enhanced rate` EQUALS `the higher rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled to child disability payment with the care component at the highest rate` EQUALS `the higher rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance with the care component at the highest rate` EQUALS `the higher rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled to personal independence payment with the daily living component at the enhanced rate` EQUALS `the higher rate`
-- (b)(ii): a child who is blind gets the higher rate whether or not entitled to a benefit.
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a blind child entitled to no benefit` EQUALS `the higher rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child certified as blind but not by a consultant ophthalmologist` EQUALS `no additional amount`
-- Benefits outside limb (a): attendance allowance and carer's allowance do not give the lower rate.
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled only to attendance allowance` EQUALS `no additional amount`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `a child entitled only to carer's allowance` EQUALS `no additional amount`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2)(a) — entitled to a benefit that gives the lower rate` `a child entitled to child disability payment with the care component at the highest rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2)(a) — entitled to a benefit that gives the lower rate` `a child entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance with the care component at the highest rate`
#ASSERT `reg 24(2)(a) — entitled to a benefit that gives the lower rate` `a child entitled to adult disability payment with the daily living component at the enhanced rate`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 24(2)(a) — entitled to a benefit that gives the lower rate` `a blind child entitled to no benefit`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 25: the payment, liability and occupation conditions.
#ASSERT `reg 25(2) — the payment condition` (`Payments in respect of accommodation` WITH `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1` IS TRUE, `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 25(2) — the payment condition` (`Payments in respect of accommodation` WITH `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1` IS FALSE, `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(2) — the payment condition` (`Payments in respect of accommodation` WITH `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1` IS FALSE, `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1` IS FALSE))

`liable on a commercial basis` MEANS `Liability of a claimant to make payments in respect of accommodation` WITH
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis` IS TRUE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments` IS FALSE
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments` IS FALSE
`treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` MEANS `Liability of a claimant to make payments in respect of accommodation` WITH
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis` IS FALSE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments` IS TRUE
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments` IS FALSE
`liable on a commercial basis but treated as not liable by Part 2 of Schedule 2` MEANS `Liability of a claimant to make payments in respect of accommodation` WITH
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis` IS TRUE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments` IS FALSE
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments` IS TRUE
`not liable on any basis` MEANS `Liability of a claimant to make payments in respect of accommodation` WITH
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis` IS FALSE
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments` IS FALSE
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 25(3) — the liability condition` `liable on a commercial basis`
#ASSERT `reg 25(3) — the liability condition` `treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(3) — the liability condition` `liable on a commercial basis but treated as not liable by Part 2 of Schedule 2`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(3) — the liability condition` `not liable on any basis`)

`occupying the home` MEANS `Occupation of accommodation by a claimant` WITH
    `the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home` IS TRUE
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treats the claimant as not occupying that accommodation` IS FALSE
`occupying the home but treated as not occupying by Part 2 of Schedule 3` MEANS `Occupation of accommodation by a claimant` WITH
    `the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home` IS TRUE
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treats the claimant as not occupying that accommodation` IS TRUE
`not occupying the home` MEANS `Occupation of accommodation by a claimant` WITH
    `the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home` IS FALSE
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treats the claimant as not occupying that accommodation` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 25(4) — the occupation condition` `occupying the home`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(4) — the occupation condition` `occupying the home but treated as not occupying by Part 2 of Schedule 3`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(4) — the occupation condition` `not occupying the home`)

`rent payments only` MEANS `Payments in respect of accommodation` WITH
    `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1` IS TRUE
    `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1` IS FALSE
-- (5)(b) meets all of the conditions only when it meets each of the three.
#ASSERT `reg 25(5)(b) — the claimant meets all of the conditions specified in this regulation` `rent payments only` `liable on a commercial basis` `occupying the home`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(5)(b) — the claimant meets all of the conditions specified in this regulation` `rent payments only` `not liable on any basis` `occupying the home`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 25(5)(b) — the claimant meets all of the conditions specified in this regulation` `rent payments only` `liable on a commercial basis` `not occupying the home`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 26(6): a shared ownership tenancy.
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      lease IS A BOOLEAN
      `joint owners` IS A BOOLEAN
      purchase IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Tenancy that may be a shared ownership tenancy`
`test — a tenancy in` nation lease `joint owners` purchase MEANS
    `Tenancy that may be a shared ownership tenancy` WITH
        `nation in which the accommodation is` IS nation
        `a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it` IS lease
        `an agreement under which the tenant, who with the landlord jointly owns the accommodation, is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest` IS `joint owners`
        `an agreement under which the tenant has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it` IS purchase
#ASSERT `reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` (`test — a tenancy in` England TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` (`test — a tenancy in` Wales TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` (`test — a tenancy in` England FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` (`test — a tenancy in` Wales FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` (`test — a tenancy in` Scotland FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` (`test — a tenancy in` Scotland FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` (`test — a tenancy in` Scotland TRUE FALSE FALSE))

-- Regulation 26(2) to (4): which Schedules have effect.
#ASSERT `reg 26(2) to (4) — the Schedules that have effect` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Schedule 4 only`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2) to (4) — the Schedules that have effect` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Schedule 5 only`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2) to (4) — the Schedules that have effect` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `both Schedules 4 and 5, for a shared ownership tenancy`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2) to (4) — the Schedules that have effect` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply but the tenancy is not a shared ownership tenancy`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2) to (4) — the Schedules that have effect` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `neither Schedule, because the claimant does not meet all the conditions of regulation 25`
#ASSERT `reg 26(2) to (4) — the Schedules that have effect` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: neither paragraph (2) nor paragraph (3) applies`

-- (4) and (5): the amount, with the amounts under the Schedules supplied (400 under Schedule 4, 250 under Schedule 5).
#ASSERT `reg 26(4) — the amount of the housing costs element` `Schedule 4 only` 400 250 EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `reg 26(4) — the amount of the housing costs element` `Schedule 5 only` 400 250 EQUALS JUST 250
#ASSERT `reg 26(4) — the amount of the housing costs element` `both Schedules 4 and 5, for a shared ownership tenancy` 400 250 EQUALS JUST 650
#ASSERT `reg 26(4) — the amount of the housing costs element` `neither Schedule, because the claimant does not meet all the conditions of regulation 25` 400 250 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 26(4) — the amount of the housing costs element` `not covered: both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply but the tenancy is not a shared ownership tenancy` 400 250 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 26(4) — the amount of the housing costs element` `not covered: neither paragraph (2) nor paragraph (3) applies` 400 250 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 26(5) — the amount for the service charge payments is calculated under Schedule 4` `both Schedules 4 and 5, for a shared ownership tenancy` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(5) — the amount for the service charge payments is calculated under Schedule 4` `both Schedules 4 and 5, for a shared ownership tenancy` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 26(5) — the amount for the service charge payments is calculated under Schedule 4` `Schedule 4 only` TRUE)
